2026-11-13T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2492) 'the motion matching guest predicts a body on the wire
 # uuid: 41071212-cd58-543d-a4e6-24afca0afa2e
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l1
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-13T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2492) 'a sender states a clip and a time and sends only what the guest cannot predict.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2492) 'the presence slice's frame codec: a predictor under Zstandard, its gates and controls.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Both ends of a presence stream hold the same clips and the same motion matching guest. How many bytes of a body does a sender still have to send?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2492) 'A person's body goes on the wire as 21 entity Packets of 100 bytes, in two frames of 12, once every 6 ticks of a 64 Hz clock. Each frame is coded alone against one fixed dictionary. Measured on 62 clips, that stream is 8,693 bytes a second at level 19, which is 6% over the sustained budget of 8,192. A dictionary cannot close the gap: coding a frame against the send before it saves 3%. But the body is not free motion. The stick feeds `mm_step`, which answers a clip and a time, and the body is that clip's pose placed in the world. A viewer that runs the same guest on the same clips can make most of that pose itself.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Run the frame size tool on the 62 clips with the predictor in the codec and without it. The rung passes when the bytes a second with the predictor are below the 8,693 of the fixed dictionary on the same sends, the decoded frames equal the frames that were sent, bit for bit, and each of the four controls below is caught.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2492) 'the motion matching guest predicts a body on the wire
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The predictor is the motion matching guest, `mm.elf` (operator, 2026-11-13: "he motion matching guest yes."). No learned model is brought in before this has been tried.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The predictor sits in the frame codec, under Zstandard. A decoded frame is still 12 whole Packets of 100 bytes, so the Packet layout does not change and the observers hash the same frames as today.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The clip and the time travel in the payload of a Packet that is already sent. Nothing travels beside the Packets.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Every send states its own clip and time. A frame stands alone, and a lost send does not make the next one unreadable.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The hash of the clip set and of the guest joins the hashes of the dictionary and of the part table as one protocol version. A viewer with another version is refused.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2492) '- RFD66606-2436, presence, the slice this codec serves.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2492) '- RFD66606-2442 and RFD66606-2443, the latency metric and the server that carries the frames.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Start here
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2492) 'This RFD is written so that a session with no memory of the work can begin from it. Read these in order before writing anything.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The gates repository, interactor-presence-gates in our organisation. Read `docs/wire.md` for frames and Packets, `docs/frame-sizes.md` for the measurement this RFD must beat, `docs/ledger.md` with `ledger.tsv` for how a rung is recorded, and `tools/frame_sizes.exs`, the tool that measures any recorded stream. The parts it joins are repositories of their own beside it; the Packet codec is interactor-packets-guest and RFD66606-2493 names the rest.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The motion matching guest's repository, interactor-motion-matching-guest, which the workspace checks out on its interactor side. Its README has `mm_add_clip`, `mm_bake` and `mm_step(dt, vx, vz, facing, mode, jump)`, which answers a clip, a time, the character and the clip root for each frame.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The packet contract, contract-entity-packet. A Packet is 100 bytes: `gid` at 0, position in micrometres at 4, velocity at 28, acceleration at 34, the tick at 40, rotation at 52 and 40 bytes of payload at 58.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The avatar follower, interactor-anny-follow-guest. `follow.sgd` and `data/drive.tsv` hold the 21 bodies of the muscle skeleton that drive ANNY. Their order on the wire is `data/parts.tsv` of the codec's repository, a whole coarse body in the first frame.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2492) 'What was measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The 62 clips that pass the retarget gates, 29 minutes of motion, were played at the tick and written as the frames one person would send. Half the clips built the dictionary and sends of the other half were measured.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2492) '| Cadence | Dictionary | Level | Bytes a send | Bytes a second |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2492) '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | none | 3 | 982 | 10,476 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | fixed, 64 KiB | 3 | 947 | 10,100 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | fixed, 64 KiB | 19 | 815 | 8,693 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 6 ticks | the send before | 19 | 791 | 8,436 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2492) '| 8 ticks | fixed, 64 KiB | 19 | 814 | 6,510 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The row to beat is the third. The fourth shows why a better dictionary is not the way: the best possible one, the send before, gains 3%.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Why a predictor should work here
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2492) 'A body in this slice is made in a chain. The left stick sets a wanted ground velocity. The motion matching guest picks a clip and a time. The clip's pose at that time is placed in the world, and the muscle skeleton takes it. So for a sender whose body follows the guest, clip, time and root placement fix the pose of most of the 21 parts. What they do not fix is what the guest cannot know: the tracked head and hands, and what physics adds.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2492) 'No number is claimed for the saving. A rough bound, if only the head and two hands carried information beyond clip, time and root, is 150 to 250 bytes a send against 815. It is a guess until the first rung measures it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Loss is another matter
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Zstandard is not an error-correcting code and is not used as one. Compression removes redundancy and a code for errors adds it. Loss is concealed by the curve a viewer already draws: one lost send costs nothing, and after three a part moves 7% over its top speed for one segment. A third interval of playback delay is the first remedy if loss hurts. RFD66606-2327 has the gait phase the guest matches by, and RFD66606-2363 the controllers that feed it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The ladder
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Each rung is held to the rung below it and not to the budget. The budget is where the ladder ends.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Rungs are climbed in this order and none is skipped. A rung is the run of the rung below with one thing changed. It is run on the development machine before anything is pushed, and it passes when its number is better than the rung below while its controls are caught.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2492) '0. Run `tools/frame_sizes.exs` as it is on the 62 clips. Nothing has to improve: it must give 8,693 again, so that the baseline is this session's own.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2492) '1. The guest's digest on four hosts, as the MuJoCo guest has. Hosts that agree on `mm_step` go from 0 to 4.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2492) '2. Residual frames: each Packet's fields less the predicted pose, for clips played back as they are. Bytes a second go below rung 0.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2492) '3. Clip and time in a payload, and the decoder that rebuilds the frame from them. Frames rebuilt bit for bit go from none to all.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2492) '4. A body that strays from the clip: head and hands on a recorded track. Bytes a second are set against rung 2 and reported as they are.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2492) '5. The codec as a sandbox guest beside `curve.sgd`. Its bytes equal the tool's.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Rung 1 comes before any coding because a predictor that differs between two machines by one bit makes every decoded frame wrong. The MuJoCo guest already has a digest on Linux x86_64, Linux arm64, Windows x86_64 and macOS arm64, with the in-process JIT switched off, and that check found a defect on its first day.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Gates and controls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Each gate prints a `RESULT:` line, and each control plants a defect that must be caught and named.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Round trip: every frame that is coded decodes to the bytes that were sent. Control: one bit of the residual flipped.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Alone: a frame decodes with no other frame at hand. Control: a decoder that keeps the clip and time of the send before, which must fail when a send is withheld.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Version: a viewer whose clip set differs is refused by name. Control: one clip altered.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Bytes: the stream is smaller than the rung below on the same sends. Control: a predictor that answers the rest pose, which must give no saving.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2492) 'Rules a new session must keep
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The Packet stays 100 bytes and a frame stays 12 Packets. New data goes into a payload.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2492) '- New guest code is SafeGDScript first. Mojo is also a guest language (RFD66606-2494, operator, 2026-11-14). Tools are `.exs` and gates are `.gd`. No new Python.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Comments are at most 3% of a file's lines. The explanation goes into documentation.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Commits are authored as the operator, in sentence case, with no trailer and no agent credit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2492) '- No file names the reference social VR platform.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2492) '- CI confirms and does not find out: one finished pull request at a time, after the gate and its controls have passed on the development machine. No draft pull requests.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Meshes are OpenUSD only. The clips come from a private repository whose release awaits a provenance check, and they are cleared for this work.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2492) 'What is not known
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Whether `mm_step` is bit-identical across the four hosts. Nothing has run.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2492) '- How far a real player strays from the clips. Only play in a headset shows it, and the bytes of rung 4 are a first estimate.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2492) '- The time to code a frame with the predictor. The tick has about 1.8 ms to spare on the interpreted tier, so the codec may have to run off the tick.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2492) '- Whether rotation needs its own residual form. The Packet carries rotation in a swing-twist code, and a small error there may not be a small number.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2492) 'The stream is over its budget, the dictionary is spent, and the chosen cadence was kept twice by the operator. What is left is to stop sending what both ends already know.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2492  1 LINE
 Text:Written

